254
00:13:47,140 --> 00:13:49,717
play dual monsters until
we get to Battle City?

255
00:13:49,800 --> 00:13:51,420
Well, I guess so.

256
00:13:51,660 --> 00:13:52,680
Now, let's see.

257
00:13:53,220 --> 00:13:56,997
I think you know this, but when two
monsters are battling each other,

258
00:13:57,080 --> 00:13:58,897
the one with the highest
attack points wins.

259
00:13:58,980 --> 00:14:03,477
Another rule is that some monsters are so
strong, you can't play them right away.

260
00:14:03,560 --> 00:14:06,940
You have to sacrifice one or
more weaker monsters first.

261
00:14:08,020 --> 00:14:12,537
And you can tell how powerful a monster
is by counting how many stars it has.

262
00:14:12,620 --> 00:14:17,197
The more stars that you see in the bottom
of the card, the stronger the monster is.

263
00:14:17,280 --> 00:14:19,777
There are stars all
over the monster cards?

264
00:14:19,860 --> 00:14:22,160
They must look so pretty, huh, Tristan?

265
00:14:22,680 --> 00:14:24,640
Well, yeah, I guess they do.

266
00:14:24,980 --> 00:14:26,240
And one more thing.

267
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:28,618
You can fuse your monsters together.

268
00:14:28,980 --> 00:14:31,686
But to do that, you need
a special magic card.

269
00:14:31,800 --> 00:14:34,460
It's called Polymerization, and it rocks.

270
00:14:34,640 --> 00:14:37,980
So, sacrificing and
polymerization. That's right.

271
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:39,430
Cool.

272
00:14:39,513 --> 00:14:40,343
Thanks, Tristan.

273
00:14:42,220 --> 00:14:47,560
So I have to sacrifice my weak monster
to summon a stronger one. Well,

274
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:51,377
that means if I want to summon
the strong monster in my hand,

275
00:14:51,460 --> 00:14:54,401
I have to get rid of my
weaker Lady Panther first.

276
00:14:54,660 --> 00:14:57,072
Maybe this game isn't so tough after all.

277
00:14:57,200 --> 00:14:58,420
So here goes.

278
00:14:59,340 --> 00:15:04,560
I sacrificed Lady Panther so I
can summon Marie, the Fallen One.

279
00:15:06,360 --> 00:15:07,190
Good.

280
00:15:08,140 --> 00:15:12,597
I hope Serenity's getting the hang of
this, because if she messes this up now,

281
00:15:12,680 --> 00:15:15,240
Nesbit will win the duel in his next turn.

282
00:15:17,340 --> 00:15:19,220
I've got the monsters I want.

283
00:15:19,460 --> 00:15:24,180
Now I need that Polymerization card so
I can fuse them together. Serenity. Huh?

284
00:15:24,520 --> 00:15:25,440
Was that you?

285
00:15:25,720 --> 00:15:27,057
Fear not, Serenity.

286
00:15:27,140 --> 00:15:32,920
As your deckmaster, I carry with me a
very special ability, the power of fusion.

287
00:15:33,400 --> 00:15:36,517
I have the ability to combine
two or more of your monsters

288
00:15:36,600 --> 00:15:39,940
together without the need
for a polymerization card.

289
00:15:41,240 --> 00:15:46,180
But you must discard one magic card
in order to activate my ability.

290
00:15:48,820 --> 00:15:52,457
Okay, now feast your eyes on
this little number, Nesbitt.

291
00:15:52,540 --> 00:15:54,960
First I'll dispose of this,

292
00:15:55,200 --> 00:15:58,920
so then I can activate the
special ability of my Deckmaster.

293
00:16:00,600 --> 00:16:02,380
Fusion vision, go!

294
00:16:02,680 --> 00:16:04,017
Got it with the third eye?

295
00:16:04,100 --> 00:16:08,960
Fuse together Marie the Fallen One and
the Forgiving Maiden to form St. Joan!

296
00:16:12,860 --> 00:16:17,460
Impressive, but I'm afraid your monster
isn't powerful enough to take me on.

297
00:16:18,820 --> 00:16:20,060
What's going on?

298
00:16:20,260 --> 00:16:21,240
This can't be!

299
00:16:26,260 --> 00:16:27,090
Awesome!

300
00:16:27,360 --> 00:16:29,740
Command Angel's special power kicked in.

301
00:16:29,960 --> 00:16:34,254
It raised the strength of every fairy
monster on the field, including St.

302
00:16:34,380 --> 00:16:35,210
Joan.

303
00:16:35,293 --> 00:16:38,880
Thanks to Tristan's monster card,
we can still do this. Now her St.

304
00:16:39,020 --> 00:16:41,100
Joan has 3,200 attack points.

305
00:16:41,460 --> 00:16:45,220
Yeah, but his perfect machine
king still has more points. St.

306
00:16:45,560 --> 00:16:46,937
Joan needs another power boost.

307
00:16:47,020 --> 00:16:48,720
But how can she get that?

308
00:16:49,700 --> 00:16:50,557
Tristan's card!

309
00:16:50,640 --> 00:16:52,620
Hey, guys! Listen!

310
00:16:52,940 --> 00:16:57,357
I think I know how you can do this, but
you're going to need Tristan's help!

311
00:16:57,440 --> 00:16:58,560
Trust me on this!

312
00:16:58,820 --> 00:17:00,640
How can Tristan help us?

313
00:17:01,220 --> 00:17:02,080
He's not.

314
00:17:02,240 --> 00:17:03,358
Well, you guys not.

315
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:04,638
No more discussion.

316
00:17:04,980 --> 00:17:06,200
Make your move now!

317
00:17:06,940 --> 00:17:08,580
What's Yugi talking about?

318
00:17:09,360 --> 00:17:10,860
Ugh! That's it!

319
00:17:11,100 --> 00:17:13,924
Tristan still has a card
face down on the field!

320
00:17:14,040 --> 00:17:15,260
It's our last hope!

321
00:17:15,500 --> 00:17:18,117
I'm putting all my faith in that card!

322
00:17:18,200 --> 00:17:22,900
Now I activate my Deckmaster's
special ability. What?

323
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:25,500
Strike Ninja, do your stuff.

324
00:17:25,860 --> 00:17:29,440
Activate the card Tristan left
face down on the field. No.

325
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:32,040
I just gotta ditch two cards first.

326
00:17:32,300 --> 00:17:35,359
And hope that Tristan left
us something worth using.

327
00:17:35,820 --> 00:17:37,920
I guess it's time to find out now.

328
00:17:38,140 --> 00:17:39,140
This better work.

329
00:17:39,280 --> 00:17:40,520
Go, Strike Ninja.

330
00:17:40,780 --> 00:17:42,520
Raise his face down card.

331
00:17:53,400 --> 00:17:56,180
He left us rare metal soul! Awesome!

332
00:17:56,440 --> 00:17:58,217
Looks like Tristan came through.

333
00:17:58,300 --> 00:17:59,720
Too bad for Nesbitt.

334
00:18:00,280 --> 00:18:02,000
Rare metal soul raises St.

335
00:18:02,120 --> 00:18:04,200
Jones' attack points by 1,000!

336
00:18:08,380 --> 00:18:09,560
That's impossible!

337
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:11,901
Now their attack points are tied!

338
00:18:12,120 --> 00:18:13,700
What happens? Just watch!

339
00:18:14,280 --> 00:18:15,977
Okay, do the honors, Serenity,

340
00:18:16,060 --> 00:18:21,340
and get rid of this rusty old pile of
junk once and for all. All right. Go, St.

341
00:18:21,500 --> 00:18:24,380
Joan, and attack the
perfect Machine King now!

342
00:18:45,900 --> 00:18:50,547
Since Perfect Machine King was the
Deckmaster, he automatically loses the duel.

343
00:18:50,700 --> 00:18:52,480
Yeah, way to go, sis.

344
00:18:53,280 --> 00:18:54,260
You fools.

345
00:18:54,520 --> 00:18:57,680
I may be going offline,
but I want Tristan's body.

346
00:18:58,240 --> 00:18:59,880
You can't do this.

347
00:19:00,020 --> 00:19:02,540
Hey, let him go, you creep. Negative.

348
00:19:02,960 --> 00:19:05,431
He's my ticket out of this virtual prison.

349
00:19:05,780 --> 00:19:07,080
I'm finally free.

350
00:19:16,080 --> 00:19:18,460
That mechanical snake in the grass.

351
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:22,680
I don't believe it.

352
00:19:23,040 --> 00:19:24,540
They have his body.

353
00:19:24,800 --> 00:19:26,320
And it's my fault.

354
00:19:26,960 --> 00:19:28,607
Serenity, are you all right?

355
00:19:32,460 --> 00:19:34,640
It's okay, sis. Really.

356
00:19:36,740 --> 00:19:38,697
Joey, we won the match.

357
00:19:38,780 --> 00:19:41,700
Why didn't that bring
Tristan back? I don't know.

358
00:19:41,960 --> 00:19:42,920
We'll find him.

359
00:19:43,700 --> 00:19:47,347
They took Tristan's body, but
his mind must be here somewhere.

360
00:19:47,840 --> 00:19:50,369
I'm glad we're all back
together, you guys.

361
00:19:50,640 --> 00:19:52,111
Now we just need Tristan.

362
00:19:59,780 --> 00:20:00,610
Huh?

363
00:20:00,693 --> 00:20:01,620
Where am I?

364
00:20:14,660 --> 00:20:16,719
You're the only one who's competing
